• To provide our guests with exceptional breakfast, lunch, and dinner experiences;
• To take orders, provide information about menu and dishes, deliver excellent service and handle the settling of bills;
• Carry out preparation of service including mise en place;
• Assist the Food & Beverage team of the hotel with set up and service.As Waiter/ Waitress we expect from you: 
• Prior experience in similar positions at high-end restaurants;
• Excellent knowledge of English language (written and spoken);
• Flexibility to different shift patterns, including mornings, evenings and weekend shifts.  Our commitment to you:
• A salary in scale IV of the Dutch Horeca CAO;
• Excellent career progression with an iconic, luxury, global hotel brand. A lot of our colleagues joined us at the beginning of their career and are now leading their own teams and divisions;
• Fantastic learning and development opportunities for all levels of staff, with targeted development programs to get you ready for the next step in your career;
• Discounted stays at our beautiful properties across the Group;
• Multiple additional benefits, such as supplemented staff meals, uniform/laundry service, ticket raffles a

SamenvattingDo you prefer working at night, staying active, and would you like to be part of one of the world's largest logistics companies? Then be sure to read on! Good Work!Over de functieAs a Warehouse Employee, you ensure that parcels are sorted and scanned. You are therefore an important link in the logistics process! This is an active job that involves a lot of walking and lifting.
- Loading and unloading parcels from trucks;
- Sorting parcels by destination and size;
- Scanning parcels and updating tracking systems;
- Reporting damaged or suspicious parcels.

This job is for 20–25 hours per week. The shifts are night shifts on weekdays.
Working hours:
You start between 2:00 AM and 3:00 AM and finish between 6:00 AM and 10:00 AM, usually around 8:00 AM.
Over het bedrijfYour new employer, DHL, is an indispensable link in the global logistics process. Parcels are sorted, shipped, and delivered in more than 200 countries.
Wat wij vragen- Own accomodation in The Netherlands;
- You speak basic Dutch or English;
- You are in good physical condition and able to lift heavy items;
- You are available to work night shifts.

Of course, these points are essential for the role of order picker, but we are primarily interested in who you are! Inspire us.
Wat wij bieden- A salary of €14,99 gross per hour;
- 130% allowance on top of your salary for working in the night;
- 150% allowance if you work overtime;
- 200% pay for working on public holidays;
- 8% holiday allowance;
- Opportunities for career growth and professional development.

Meer informatieAre you interested in the job of Warehouse Employee? You can apply within 2 minutes. Do you have some questions first? Kamila answers them via +31625477379 and k.spiewak@carriere.com. Good work!
